Expected elements: present

All must-show items are on the page: provenance banner above the identity bar (badge, `aztec` slug, producer sentences), identity bar with a chain-targeted exit, truncated hash, `Partial`, block, four stepping groups, scrubber, position readout and phase rail; Code pane positioned at line 32; Call Trace and Event Log as one tabbed region with Call Trace open and seven frames; Values as a separate pane below with eleven values; Transaction metadata pane. No forbidden item: no spinner, no empty pane, no full-width pane row, no prose band above the panes, Values is not a tab. The `NOIR` tag is correct here and the cost row reads cleanly.

As a density surface this is strong in the rows it fills — the ACIR column is tabular and right-aligned, changed values are marked, inline value chips are excellent — but it spends its scarcest resource badly. 178px (16.5% of the viewport) goes above the first pane, and the banner sets four lines at a 580px measure inside a 1904px band, leaving roughly 1330x130px blank. The call-trace region is 47% empty below its last frame while the Code and Transaction panes are both cut off at the viewport bottom. Two metadata rows carry only `0x` under prose claiming raw bytes are shown.

Highest-priority fixes: give the Values pane the height the call-trace region is not using, and widen the banner's measure to return ~60px to the panes.

Rating: 6/10

